<!-- [EN Sync v7.0] -->
<div class="lf-trap-card" data-trap="T1" data-hq-id="LF-T1-AI">
            <div class="lf-trap-header">
                <span class="lf-trap-badge">T1</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-diff">⭐⭐</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-id">LF-T1-AI</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Xiao Ming has 120 yuan. He uses half of the money to buy books, and then uses 1/3 of the remaining money to buy stationery. How much money does he have left at the end?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake</span>
                    <span >120 ÷ 2 = 60, 60 ÷ 3 = 20, 20 yuan left.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-right">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Approach</span>
                    <span >First use half: 120 ÷ 2 = 60 yuan (60 yuan left after buying books). Then use 1/3 of the remaining: 60 × 1/3 = 20 yuan (20 yuan used for stationery). Finally left: 60 - 20 = 40 yuan.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-note">💡 "1/3 of the remaining" means subtract from what's left, not directly divide by 3.</div>
            </div>
        </div>
<div class="lf-trap-card" data-trap="T2" data-hq-id="LF-T2-AI">
            <div class="lf-trap-header">
                <span class="lf-trap-badge">T2</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-diff">⭐⭐⭐</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-id">LF-T2-AI</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">A rectangular garden has a length of 15 meters and a width of 8 meters. If trees are planted along the edge of the garden every 2 meters, with trees at all four corners, how many trees are needed in total?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake</span>
                    <span >(15+8)×2 = 46 meters, 46 ÷ 2 = 23 trees.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-right">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Approach</span>
                    <span >First calculate the perimeter: (15+8)×2 = 46 meters. Since it is a closed shape with trees at all four corners, number of trees = perimeter ÷ spacing = 46 ÷ 2 = 23 trees. Note: For a closed shape, no need to add 1.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-note">💡 For planting trees on a closed shape, number of trees = perimeter ÷ spacing, no need to add 1.</div>
            </div>
        </div>
</body>
</html>